WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.270
Yamato or Carrot?

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.720
Bon Clay or Vivi?

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.920
Katakuri or Smoker?

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:13.679
The One Piece community absolutely loves to
debate potential candidates to join the Straw

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:19.830
hat Crew, so today we are going to rank them
all from the absolute worst fits to the ones

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:23.640
that definitely should already be a Straw
Hat.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.320
One thing you may not know though is that
there are actually pretty strict requirements

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.780
about which characters get to join the crew.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:35.160
These three requirements are NEVER broken,
and each member fulfills all three.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.800
They are: 1.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.110
Every straw hat has a tragic backstory. 2.

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:44.050
Every straw hat has a dream that can be fulfilled
by joining the crew.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.050
And 3.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:49.090
every straw hat must have an actual role on
the crew.

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:54.219
And just to show you what I mean, Chopper
was abandoned as a young Reindeer, then he

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:57.600
poisoned his friend, which is pretty tragic
if you ask me.

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.090
Next, we have Chopper’s dream, which is
to be able to cure any disease.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:05.110
Then obviously his role is the crew’s doctor.

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:09.570
And these three requirements hold true for
every single straw hat, which means that some

00:01:09.570 --> 00:01:14.450
of these characters we are about to rank would
make absolutely no sense to join the crew,

00:01:14.450 --> 00:01:17.860
while others are actually pretty perfect.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:23.500
Let’s kick this off with the absolute worst
candidate that fans thought might join the

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.580
crew because at number eighteen we have the
Gassy scientist, Caesar Clown.

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:35.579
Which yes, sounds crazy, but there was a time
that people thought he might actually become

00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:37.750
a straw hat.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:42.500
We first met him as the main villain of the
Punk Hazard arc, and of course he did some

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:48.040
awful things which we will never forgive him
for, like kidnapping children and experimenting

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.040
on them.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:52.659
Later on though, he proved pretty helpful
to the crew, like when he helped everyone

00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:54.420
escape Big Mom’s tea party.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:02:01.320
So let’s just pretend that somehow he was
let into the crew, how would he fit as a member

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.380
of the Straw Hats?

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:07.539
Well, first of all we already know that Nami
would never get along with Caesar for kidnapping

00:02:07.539 --> 00:02:11.470
and experimenting on innocent children and
creating weapons of mass destruction.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.480
However, his usefulness as a scientist is
impossible to ignore.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.069
He easily helped heal the poisoned minks on
Zou and he also helped Chopper improve his

00:02:21.069 --> 00:02:22.350
rumble ball technology.

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:28.069
So yeah, he could be pretty handy to have
around, but he’s still a scumbag and the

00:02:28.069 --> 00:02:29.930
crew will never let him on.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:35.010
And just slightly above Caesar is another
former villain who has actually traveled on

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:39.690
board the ship multiple times, which is the
Swamp man Caribou.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:45.050
And I promise, these candidates will get WAY
better as we go down the rankings, but Caribou

00:02:45.050 --> 00:02:50.140
is another straight up evil dude who spends
most of his time trying to kidnap mermaids

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:52.019
to sell at the slave auction.

00:02:52.019 --> 00:02:58.170
Which is pretty messed up, and should pretty
much make him an auto-reject to join the crew.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:03.360
Somehow though he keeps ending up on the ship,
even after we leave Wano, which has led some

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:06.500
people to wonder if he could eventually join
the crew.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:12.090
But for the purpose of this video, he would
honestly be pretty useful to have on the crew.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:17.030
I mean his logia swamp powers act as a sort
of pocket dimension, so he could sneak the

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.660
entire crew into places they might not be
able to reach.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:25.870
Beyond his Logia power though, he is pretty
weak and could probably be defeated by any

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:31.209
decent fight with haki, plus he has no real
role on the crew.

00:03:31.209 --> 00:03:34.800
So, goodbye creepy swamp man.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:39.720
The candidates are about to get WAY BETTER
though because next up is Gaimon.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:44.960
And it has been a LONG TIME since we saw the
most beautiful afro in the story, because

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:50.819
Luffy, Zoro, and Nami stopped at his island
way back before they rescued Usopp’s hometown.

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:57.159
And now this happened over twenty-five years
ago, which is way before most of us were reading

00:03:57.159 --> 00:04:00.700
or watching One Piece, but it’s pretty easy
to make a good case for Gaimon joining the

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:01.700
crew.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:05.700
I mean at this point in the story, Luffy was
picking up a crewmate from every island he

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.200
stopped at, so it would be reasonable to think
Gaimon would join as well.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:15.080
And with his love for treasure chests, Gaimon
would have been a perfect crewmate to be in

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:19.450
charge of the crew’s money and gold, so
basically a treasurer.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:24.050
Besides that though, he is not really a fighter,
although maybe he could have been some kind

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:25.930
of powerful animal trainer???

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:31.020
Anyway, none of these candidates so far would
have affected the Straw Hat’s story much

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:38.139
at all, but that all changes with our next
candidate, MontBlanc Cricket.

00:04:38.139 --> 00:04:43.300
Now when we first met Cricket, he was living
on the edge of Jaya, searching for the legendary

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.449
city of gold.

00:04:44.449 --> 00:04:49.860
And while the Straw Hats eventually found
the golden city up in the sky, Cricket was

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:54.360
at one point considered to be a possible new
member to join the crew.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:05:00.140
And honestly, he could perfectly fill a super
important role, which is that of the log book

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:01.140
keeper.

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:05.199
Because as we saw during the samurai Oden’s
flashback, it is super important for someone

00:05:05.199 --> 00:05:09.850
on the crew to keep track of the crew’s
journey so that people who come after can

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.330
know what truly happened.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:14.930
And well, the straw hats have never had that.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:20.009
So if Cricket had joined the crew this could
have changed the way the entire world views

00:05:20.009 --> 00:05:21.009
the Straw Hats.

00:05:21.009 --> 00:05:25.490
For example, I can just imagine Cricket keeping
records of the crew’s adventures and those

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:30.699
records somehow being shared with the world,
so that everyone would know just how good

00:05:30.699 --> 00:05:32.720
the Straw Hat crew really are.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:38.319
And even though it didn’t happen, I’m
a bit sad that this chestnut-head dude didn’t

00:05:38.319 --> 00:05:39.569
join the crew.

00:05:39.569 --> 00:05:44.510
Which is the EXACT OPPOSITE of how I feel
about this next candidate.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:52.360
That’s because Rebecca was heavily speculated
to be joining the crew during the entire Dressrosa

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:53.360
arc.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:56.900
And honestly, there were a ton of characters
people thought might actually join the crew

00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:01.650
during this arc, but Rebecca is the one I
always heard about most.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:07.099
And even though she is a decent fighter with
her expert sword skills, she isn’t strong

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:13.000
enough to make a difference in any major fights,
and I’d even rank her below even the weakest

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.000
straw hats.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:18.230
She also doesn’t have any clear role on
the crew, and we certainly don’t need any

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:23.199
more scenes of her crying since we had SO
MANY of those during Dressrosa.

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:26.039
Now this next candidate might surprise you.

00:06:26.039 --> 00:06:32.289
Because this person is the first of many marines
who at one time we thought might join the

00:06:32.289 --> 00:06:33.289
crew.

00:06:33.289 --> 00:06:38.870
This is of course Koby, who was literally
the first person that Luffy met after setting

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:39.880
out on his adventure.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:47.590
Now, Koby has changed quite a bit over the
years, but he is almost THE PERFECT straw

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:49.840
hat candidate if you think about it.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:55.259
He has a tragic backstory where he was forced
to be a slave for years.

00:06:55.259 --> 00:07:01.229
He has grown incredibly powerful, so if he
were to join the crew it could be as a strong

00:07:01.229 --> 00:07:02.229
fighter like Zoro.

00:07:02.229 --> 00:07:08.500
But it is actually Koby's determination to
pursue his dream of being a Marine Admiral

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:13.319
that will ALWAYS prevent Koby from being a
straw hat.

00:07:13.319 --> 00:07:19.000
Because he is never likely to become a pirate,
and no pirate means no straw hat crewmate.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:22.960
So sorry Koby, you’ll always be a friend
though.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:28.040
And while this next candidate never fulfilled
the straw hat requirements like Koby, that

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.669
didn’t stop TONS of people from thinking
he would join the crew.

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:37.960
I’m talking about the jaguar mink Pedro,
who traveled with the Straw Hats to help save

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:40.270
Sanji during the Whole Cake Island arc.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:45.889
And it was during this time that Pedro showed
off how useful a crew mate he could be.

00:07:45.889 --> 00:07:51.169
He was incredibly intelligent, an excellent
fighter, as well as having a lot of knowledge

00:07:51.169 --> 00:07:52.740
about the New World.

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:57.611
Plus, since he didn’t get to travel with
the former pirate king, Gol D. Roger, it just

00:07:57.611 --> 00:08:03.430
made a ton of sense that he would travel with
the future pirate king by joining Luffy’s

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:04.430
crew.

00:08:04.430 --> 00:08:09.710
Unfortunately, Pedro is the one character
in this ranking who could not join because

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:16.840
of death because Pedro made the ultimate sacrifice
when he blew himself up to allow the crew

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.260
to escape from Big Mom’s territory.

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:24.319
So while we don’t know if Pedro would have
joined the crew if he lived, he was definitely

00:08:24.319 --> 00:08:28.270
a strong candidate while he was still alive.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:34.039
Though while Pedro would be a strong addition
to the crew, there is NO ONE in this entire

00:08:34.039 --> 00:08:39.209
ranking that comes close to the impact this
next candidate would have.

00:08:39.209 --> 00:08:46.950
I’m talking about the former admiral, Kuzan,
who many fans hoped would eventually join

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:50.640
the straw hats after leaving the marines during
the timeskip.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:56.190
Those hopes were ruined pretty early on though
when we learned that Kuzan had joined Blackbeard’s

00:08:56.190 --> 00:09:03.170
crew, but man it would have been INCREDIBLE
if the Ice Logia fruit user became a straw

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:04.170
hat.

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:10.910
I mean he’s pretty much one of the top fifteen
or twenty strongest characters in the story,

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:16.740
so adding him to the crew would make future
battles WAY EASIER.

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:21.779
Just take the battle against Kaido, for example,
because I’d probably rank Kuzan ABOVE Luffy

00:09:21.779 --> 00:09:24.079
before he had his Gear 5 powerup.

00:09:24.079 --> 00:09:29.410
So adding him as a fighter on the crew would
be a massive help, since he could fight top

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:35.329
commanders and even clash with Emperors, which
is extra helpful because Luffy often needs

00:09:35.329 --> 00:09:37.160
some time to rest during battles.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:41.230
However, Kuzan doesn’t really have a clear
role on the crew and we don’t actually know

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.620
what his main goals are.

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:47.190
We do know that he joined Blackbeard, but
there are always theories that he is still

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:52.779
undercover for the marines, and on top of
that Kuzan has always seemed to be trying

00:09:52.779 --> 00:09:56.870
to figure out what exactly it means to enforce
Justice.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:10:02.370
So yeah, a fun idea to think about, but Kuzan
was never really likely to join, unlike the

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:05.590
characters coming up in the rest of the ranking.

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:11.050
We can’t say the same for Paulie though,
because during the Water 7 arc, he was most

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:14.260
people’s number one option to join the straw
hats.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:19.760
I mean they were already looking for a shipwright,
which he is, and he was a decently strong

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.760
fighter.

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:25.779
Plus, I guess he has somewhat of a tragic
backstory, if you can count a huge gambling

00:10:25.779 --> 00:10:27.720
debt as tragic.

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:29.740
But in the end it just didn’t happen.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:34.010
I for one would have loved to see him on the
crew though for a few reasons.

00:10:34.010 --> 00:10:41.180
One, his Rope Action is just an awesome skill,
even though it isn’t even a devil fruit.

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:45.270
Plus he is actually pretty modest when it
comes to women, like when he demanded Nami

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:50.019
put on more clothes, so he would have been
a nice contrast against some of the more perverted

00:10:50.019 --> 00:10:51.480
gags from Sanji and Brook.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:53.769
But even Paulie cannot compare to the mind-boggling
resumes of these next straw hat candidates,

00:10:53.769 --> 00:10:54.769
and unlike every character in this ranking
you can join the crew by clicking that nice

00:10:54.769 --> 00:10:55.769
red subscribe button to get more one piece
content just like this.

00:10:55.769 --> 00:10:57.110
Man though, shoutout to our next candidate,
Kin’emon, because this man basically traveled

00:10:57.110 --> 00:11:03.190
with the crew for almost FOUR-HUNDRED CHAPTERS.

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:10.110
He has been a major part of the group ever
since we first met him as this farting pair

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:14.260
of legs back in Punk Hazard all the way up
through the end of the Wano arc.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:20.670
And being a samurai from Wano, he is a pretty
strong fighter who I’d rank around average

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:21.700
for the straw hats.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:26.269
And we don’t even need to imagine how he
would interact with the crew because he was

00:11:26.269 --> 00:11:28.370
with everyone for so long.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:32.889
He is pretty much friends with everyone, and
it would have been great to have another swordsman

00:11:32.889 --> 00:11:33.889
on the crew.

00:11:33.889 --> 00:11:37.550
Though, if I’m being honest I am glad we
don’t have his pervy personality joining

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.550
the crew.

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:43.430
However, his dream of saving his homeland
has already been accomplished, so he doesn’t

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:47.079
really meet the requirement of having a dream
anymore.

00:11:47.079 --> 00:11:51.200
That all changes though when we talk about
our next candidate.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:57.420
Because Momo has almost all of the same qualifications
as Kin’emon except even better.

00:11:57.420 --> 00:12:01.839
For starters, he traveled with the crew for
a long time just like Kin’emon, but with

00:12:01.839 --> 00:12:08.180
his recent age-up in the story, and his OP
dragon devil fruit, Momo would certainly be

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:10.589
a powerhouse fighter to add to the crew.

00:12:10.589 --> 00:12:14.680
And he even has a pretty solid dream of wanting
to explore the world, which means he could

00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:19.600
be the perfect log book keeper, just like
his father was on Gol D. Roger’s ship.

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:23.639
So yeah, he made a pretty logical choice as
a straw hat candidate.

00:12:23.639 --> 00:12:29.139
In the end though, he stayed behind as the
Shogun of Wano instead of joining the crew.

00:12:29.139 --> 00:12:34.850
And I would actually say that Momo is an even
better candidate than our next potential straw

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:41.740
hat, but I just can’t get over the fact
of how much I would have LOVED to see Katakuri

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:42.740
join the crew.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:47.190
Now, he was Luffy’s main opponent during
the Whole Cake Island arc, so you might be

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:50.610
wondering why people thought he might join
the crew.

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:55.240
The reason comes from the very end of the
marathon battle between Luffy and the donut-loving

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.240
mochi man.

00:12:56.240 --> 00:13:01.350
Because by the end of this fight, Katakuri
had become a MAJOR believer in Luffy, so much

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:05.680
so that he even seems okay with Luffy eventually
defeating his mother.

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:14.770
And this fueled a lot of speculation about
Katakuri being a future straw hat, and honestly

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:17.990
he just seems like a perfect candidate to
join the crew.

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:23.389
He’s obviously a top-tier fighter on par
with Zoro and Sanji, and his chill personality

00:13:23.389 --> 00:13:26.930
means he should get along with everyone pretty
easily.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:31.460
His mochi devil fruit could also be an infinite
food source, so no more needing Chopper as

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:36.320
emergency food, and he could easily inherit
his mother’s dream of creating a world where

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:38.220
everyone can live free.

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:43.610
He even has a tragic backstory, although being
bullied isn’t quite the same as losing your

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:48.220
parents, so he basically checks off all of
the straw hat boxes.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:54.410
Sadly though it looks like the closest we’ll
get to one of my personal favorite characters

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:57.779
joining the crew is him being a future ally.

00:13:57.779 --> 00:14:02.520
Now, before we get to the top five Straw Hat
Candidates who should have joined the crew,

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:07.029
we have another super interesting character
with Marco the Phoenix.

00:14:07.029 --> 00:14:12.980
And this fan favorite was high on everyone’s
lists of possible new crewmates when the crew

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:14.900
came out of the timeskip.

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:19.270
That’s because after the former Emperor
Whitebeard was killed and his crew mostly

00:14:19.270 --> 00:14:24.199
wiped out by Blackbeard, Marco was a free
agent.

00:14:24.199 --> 00:14:30.889
And similar to Jinbe, who did eventually join
the crew, Marco was already an ally, he was

00:14:30.889 --> 00:14:36.730
an older character who knew a ton about the
New World, and he has one of THE COOLEST devil

00:14:36.730 --> 00:14:38.570
fruits in the entire story.

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:42.769
So even though he doesn’t really fit the
tragic backstory or having a dream part of

00:14:42.769 --> 00:14:47.899
the straw hat requirements, it was always
just so much fun to think Marco might join

00:14:47.899 --> 00:14:48.990
the crew.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:53.600
Similar to Katakuri, he’s a pretty chill
dude who has already spent time with the crew.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:58.959
I bet he would especially get along with Chopper
because they are both doctors, even though

00:14:58.959 --> 00:15:02.209
Marco cheats with his devil fruit, but that’s
alright.

00:15:02.209 --> 00:15:07.430
And he would be an incredibly valuable crewmate,
with his ability to heal injuries, help the

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:12.420
crew escape with his flying, and of course
his top-tier fighting ability, which even

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:16.490
allows him to clash with admirals and top
Yonko commanders.

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:22.990
And while this next character isn’t quite
as powerful, she certainly had the fanbase

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:27.820
COMPLETELY SPLIT on if she should join the
crew or not.

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:34.260
I’m talking about the loveable rabbit, Carrot,
who played a HUGE role in helping the straw

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:36.089
hats rescue Sanji from Whole Cake Island.

00:15:36.089 --> 00:15:39.970
Then she kinda disappeared… for like most
of Wano.

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:41.839
But we’re not here to talk about that!

00:15:41.839 --> 00:15:48.079
We’re here to discuss her fit with the crew,
and honestly it’s pretty near perfect.

00:15:48.079 --> 00:15:51.699
She was great at the role of Lookout during
her time on the Sunny.

00:15:51.699 --> 00:15:54.550
Her quirky personality was right at home with
the rest of the crew.

00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:59.200
Really, though, she doesn’t have a tragic
backstory or a big dream to accomplish, so

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:03.250
I guess we shouldn’t have been too surprised
when she didn’t join the crew.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:08.079
And I have to admit, I’m far less salty
about Carrot not joining rather than the number

00:16:08.079 --> 00:16:11.449
one character coming up on the list.

00:16:11.449 --> 00:16:16.430
This next character though might be a bit
of a shocker.

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:20.560
That’s because now we have the marine Vice-Admiral
Smoker.

00:16:20.560 --> 00:16:26.930
And I know what you’re thinking, this cigar-smoking
dude is still a marine, and he’s shown no

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:30.520
signs of joining the crew, but hear me out.

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:35.120
First, Smoker has shown up many times throughout
the story on islands that the Straw Hats were

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:37.810
also on, such as Alabasta and Punk Hazard.

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:44.340
And in each place, Smoker witnessed the Straw
Hats save the country while the Marines and

00:16:44.340 --> 00:16:48.209
World Government were either powerless or
straight up didn’t care.

00:16:48.209 --> 00:16:53.540
Now, that hasn’t stopped Smoker from climbing
the marine ranks, but no matter what Smoker

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:58.740
is always trying to help normal people and
do what he believes is right.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:02.569
Which ironically enough, usually doesn’t
line up with the World Government’s way

00:17:02.569 --> 00:17:03.569
of doing things.

00:17:03.569 --> 00:17:08.039
So just wait because when the Government’s
dark secrets are finally shown to the entire

00:17:08.039 --> 00:17:14.360
world, I wouldn’t be surprised at all if
Smoker decides he’s had enough and flips

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:16.380
sides to become a pirate.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:19.020
Now, how does he fit with the Straw Hats?

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:23.169
Well, he’s already pretty familiar with
them due to their clashes in the past, and

00:17:23.169 --> 00:17:27.100
as a Smoke Logia fruit user, he’s pretty
powerful already.

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:35.740
Plus, his dream of figuring out what true
justice is and how to achieve it fits perfectly

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:39.419
with the straw hats’ destiny to free the
world.

00:17:39.419 --> 00:17:44.710
Though it’s true we don’t know if he has
a tragic backstory, and he has a pretty rough

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:48.900
personality that doesn’t exactly fit with
the crew.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:53.510
But if we keep in mind that Robin also joined
the crew as a pretty closed off individual,

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:58.250
then I’m sure someone like Smoker would
also eventually open up to the rest of the

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.250
crew.

00:17:59.250 --> 00:18:04.540
So who knows, if he’ll join later on, but
I’m not ruling out Smoker just yet.

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:09.950
Which takes us to the one character who I
don’t think ANYONE would EVER argue against

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:11.180
joining the crew.

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:14.309
And that is Mr. 2, Bon Kurei.

00:18:14.309 --> 00:18:19.370
And wow, even without the tragic backstory,
big dream, or a role on the crew, this dude

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:27.039
has literally sacrificed himself for the Straw
Hats more than anyone else in the story.

00:18:27.039 --> 00:18:30.400
He stayed behind in Alabasta so Luffy and
the others could escape.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:33.240
He saved Luffy from death by poison in Impel
Down.

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:39.540
And THEN he let himself get captured so that
the crew could escape from the underwater

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:40.540
prison.

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:48.049
I mean, what a chad, and if anyone deserves
a spot on the crew, it is THIS MAN RIGHT HERE!

00:18:48.049 --> 00:18:55.950
But even Bon Clay’s sacrifice was not nearly
as shocking as Vivi NOT JOINING the crew at

00:18:55.950 --> 00:18:57.470
the end of Alabasta.

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:59.210
I mean, wow.

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:01.600
Everyone thought she was going to join!

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:06.890
Everyone WANTED Vivi to join because she got
along so perfectly with literally everyone.

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:07.890
But no.

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:10.789
She stayed behind to take care of her country.

00:19:10.789 --> 00:19:12.700
Sad day, for sure.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:15.170
But wow, she would have been perfect.

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:19.960
First, her mom died at a young age and she
was forced to go undercover to save her kingdom,

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:22.730
so she has a tragic backstory.

00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:26.580
And I actually think she would make a perfect
Vice-Captain for the Straw Hats and could

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.550
even teach Luffy more about leadership.

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:33.470
Which might have helped in later arcs like
with the family feud between Luffy and Usopp

00:19:33.470 --> 00:19:34.470
in Water 7.

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:40.010
Unfortunately though, her dream was always
to save her country, which was basically already

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.600
accomplished.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:46.260
So besides traveling with her friends, she
didn’t really have a solid dream to follow

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:47.620
by sailing with the crew.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:56.679
So as sad as it was to see her not join, she’s
always been an honorary straw hat in my book.

00:19:56.679 --> 00:20:02.500
Which means we now HAVE TO discuss THE MOST
CONTROVERSIAL Straw Hat Candidate.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:03.500
Yamato.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:04.500
Or I mean, Oden.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:05.733
No, wait, is she back to Yamato?

00:20:05.733 --> 00:20:11.230
Anyway, she came on stronger than any other
character by straight up telling the crew

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:13.289
that she was going to join them.

00:20:13.289 --> 00:20:20.460
And honestly, Yamato checks all the boxes.

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:24.370
Her father imprisoned her for basically her
entire childhood.

00:20:24.370 --> 00:20:28.980
She would be an excellent fighter and log
book keeper, just like her idol Oden.

00:20:28.980 --> 00:20:34.400
And her dream is simply to explore the world
after being trapped by her father for all

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:35.400
their life.

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:39.580
So yeah, I thought, and pretty much most of
the fanbase thought, that she would join the

00:20:39.580 --> 00:20:41.390
crew after Wano.

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:52.540
Luffy even wanted her to join, but for some
reason she decided at the last minute to stay

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:53.540
behind.

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:55.890
However, if Yamato were to join, I think she’d
fit right in.

00:20:55.890 --> 00:21:00.169
She is certainly goofy enough to get along
with the crew’s silliness.

00:21:00.169 --> 00:21:03.150
Plus her devil fruit is just so awesome.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.590
Love the icy-wolf powers.

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:11.360
In fact, it is one of my all time favorite
devil fruits, but even Yamato’s fruit isn’t

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:16.610
as overpowered as some of the most creative
devil fruits that could break the one piece

00:21:16.610 --> 00:21:21.590
world, and if you want to see exactly which
fruits I’m talking about, you can watch

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.830
this video right here.

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:27.280
Shanks for watching, and I’ll see you in
the next one.

